  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Through the use of theorems on logarithms, \\(\\log\\dfrac ab+\\log\\dfrac bc+\\log\\dfrac cd-\\log\\dfrac{ay}{dx}\\) can be reduced to:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\log\\dfrac yx\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\log\\dfrac xy\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(1\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\log\\dfrac{a^2y}{d^2x}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Combining the logarithms gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\log\\left(\\frac ab\\frac bc\\frac cd\\frac{dx}{ay}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad=\\log\\left(\\frac ad\\frac{dx}{ay}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad=\\log\\frac xy. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine the first three logarithms by multiplying their arguments",
        "The product \\( (\\frac{a}{b})(\\frac{b}{c})(\\frac{c}{d})\\) telescopes to \\(\\frac{a}{d}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
